       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as ORD-0001: metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals.\n\nThis dose adds up to 2,550 mg/day, which is the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin. That is within the labeled limit, and it fits your patient's normal kidney function. Two things to check:\n\n- **Titration:** If the patient is new to metformin, it's usually started low (500 mg once or twice daily) and increased slowly to limit GI side effects. Confirm that starting at the maximum dose is what your team intends.\n- **Kidney function:** Recheck eGFR periodically. Also hold metformin around iodinated contrast or if the patient's kidney function worsens.\n\nReview the order with your supervising resident or attending as you normally would."
      }
